<title>USA: ValuJet Inc Q1 net shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>ValuJet Inc Q1 net shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>VALUJET, INC.</p>
<p>		    Statements of Operations (Unaudited) (In</p>
<p>thousands, except per share data and statistical summary)</p>
<p>						 Qtr ended	Qtr ended</p>
<p>						  3/31/96	   3/31/97</p>
<p>Operating revenues:</p>
<p> Passenger				    $105,569	 $ 35,115</p>
<p> Cargo					     1,446		449</p>
<p> Other					     2,980	    1,364</p>
<p> Total operating revenues		  109,995	   36,928</p>
<p>Operating expenses and other, net</p>
<p> Flight operations			     7,518	    4,103</p>
<p> Aircraft fuel				  22,076	    9,136</p>
<p> Maintenance				    15,612	   14,106</p>
<p> Station operations			   17,893	   10,353</p>
<p> Passenger services			    3,992	    1,695</p>
<p> Marketing and advertising		   4,283	    2,352</p>
<p> Sales and reservations			8,895	    3,078</p>
<p> General and administrative		  3,890	    2,796</p>
<p> Employee bonus				  1,795		  0</p>
<p> Depreciation				    6,516	    4,885</p>
<p> Gain on sale of assets			    0	     (50)</p>
<p> Shutdown and other nonrecurring exps.	 0	    9,338</p>
<p> Total operating expenses		   92,470	   61,792</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)		    17,525	 (24,864)</p>
<p>Other (income) expenses, net:</p>
<p>   Interest expenses			   2,403	    6,209</p>
<p>   Interest income			   (1,847)	  (1,566)</p>
<p> Total other (income) expenses, net	  556	    4,643</p>
<p> Income (loss) before income taxes	16,969	 (29,507)</p>
<p> Income tax (benefit) expense		6,302	 (11,000)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			    10,667	 (18,507)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share		  0.18	   (0.34)</p>
<p> Wtd. avg. shares outstanding	     59,739	   54,877</p>
<p>Statistical Summary:</p>
<p> Revenue passengers enplaned	   1,466,129	  580,700</p>
<p> Revenue passenger miles (000)	   766,637	  276,357</p>
<p> Available seat miles (000)	    1,321,617	  512,394</p>
<p> Load factor				     58.0%	    53.9%</p>
<p>Break-even load factor excluding</p>
<p>   shutdown and other nonrecurring exps.  48.5%	   85.6%</p>
<p> Average fare				    72.01	    60.47</p>
<p> Passenger yield per RPM (cents)	   13.77	    12.71</p>
<p> Total revenue per ASM (cents)		8.32	     7.21</p>
<p>Operating cost per ASM excluding</p>
<p>   shutdown and other nonrecurring exps.  7.00	    10.24</p>
<p> Operating margin				15.9%	  (67.3)%</p>
<p> Net margin					 9.7%	  (50.1)%</p>
<p>NOTE: ValuJet Inc reported a net loss for the first quarter 1997 of $18.5 million, or $0.34 per share, compared to net income of $10.7 million, or $.18 per share for the first quarter 1996. Excluding non-recurring expenses of $9.3 million resulting from maintenance and depreciation on non-performing assets, ValuJet lost $12.7 million for the quarter, or approximately $0.23 per share.</p>
